00:30:11.260 --> 00:30:20.990
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Saeed's job was to get close to Khalifa, see if he was doing more than just talking. And the FBI gave him a cover. They told him to say he was working for the Red Cross.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>赛义德的工作是接近哈利法，看他是否做了不仅仅是说话的事情。FBI给了他一个伪装。他们告诉他说他在为红十字会工作。

00:30:20.990 --> 00:30:34.600
<v Jonathan Menjivar>They set him up in a safe house, in an apartment one block from Khalifa, and he went by a different name. And just so this doesn't get confusing, from this point on in the story, we're going to refer to Saeed by that name. That name was Sharif.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>他们把他安置在一个安全屋里，就在离哈利法一个街区的地方，他换了个名字。为了不产生混淆，从故事的这一点开始，我们将用那个名字称呼赛义德。那个名字是谢里夫。

00:30:34.600 --> 00:30:47.220
<v Jonathan Menjivar>So Sharif-- again, that's Saeed undercover-- he started going to the same mosque as Khalifa. And then he actually met him. Sharif bumped into Khalifa on the street one day and introduced himself. Here's how he described Khalifa in the film.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>所以谢里夫——再强调一遍，那是卧底的赛义德——他开始去哈利法所在的清真寺。然后他真的遇到了他。谢里夫有一天在街上撞见了哈利法并作了自我介绍。他在电影中是这样描述哈利法的。

00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:55.380
<v Sharif>The way I see him running around here now, it would make any motherfucker suspicious. He's walking around looking like a Taliban.
<v Sharif>我看着他现在到处跑的样子，任何混蛋都会起疑心。他看起来就像个塔利班。

00:30:55.380 --> 00:31:09.470
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Khalifa had grown up Protestant and converted to Islam when he was 14. In 2001, he went to prison for selling drugs. It was a felony. Over the years, Khalifa had other charges, for having a gun without a license, and assault.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>哈利法是在新教环境中长大的，14岁时皈依了伊斯兰教。2001年，他因贩毒入狱。那是重罪。多年来，哈利法还有过其他指控，因为无照持枪和袭击。

00:31:09.470 --> 00:31:21.120
<v Jonathan Menjivar>And Khalifa was public about his conversion. He'd proselytize. Neighbors in his apartment building say that he'd slip Islamic brochures under their doors and take down Christmas cards they'd hung up.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>哈利法公开谈论他的皈依。他会去传教。他公寓楼里的邻居说他会把伊斯兰宣传单塞进他们的门下，并摘掉他们挂出来的圣诞贺卡。

00:31:21.120 --> 00:31:41.620
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Khalifa married a Somali woman. They had a kid. And they were getting by on welfare and money Khalifa made selling books. Some of them were books on Islam that he got from a sheik in South Africa. And he'd even started some kind of religious school. In 2006, he started holding classes in his apartment for local Somali children. Again, here's David.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>哈利法娶了一位索马里妇女。他们有一个孩子。他们依靠福利和哈利法卖书赚的钱生活。其中一些是他在南非从一个谢赫那里得到的伊斯兰书籍。他甚至开始某种宗教学校。2006年，他开始在公寓里为当地索马里儿童开设课程。再强调一次，这是大卫。

00:31:41.620 --> 00:31:52.160
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>And they called it al-Shabaab, which in Arabic means, "the youth." But it's also the name of the al-Qaeda-affiliated terrorist organization in Somalia. He wasn't aware of that at the time when he named the school.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>他们叫它“青年党”(al-Shabaab)，在阿拉伯语中意味着“青年”。但它也是索马里与基地组织有关的恐怖组织的名称。他在命名学校时并不知道这一点。

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:52.820
<v Jonathan Menjivar>He was not?
<v Jonathan Menjivar>他不知道？

00:31:52.820 --> 00:32:05.920
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>But-- he was not. He did not know that that was the name of a terrorist organization. People mentioned it to him pretty quickly afterwards and said, you know, that's probably not the best name for your school, and it's probably not a great idea to have, like, business cards that say Khalifa al-Akili, Al-Shabaab.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>但是——他不知道。他不知道那是一个恐怖组织的名字。人们在那之后很快就对他提到了这件事，并说，你知道，这可能不是你学校的最佳名字，而且印有哈利法·阿基利，“青年党”的名片可能不是个好主意。

00:32:05.920 --> 00:32:12.050
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>But he was kind of defiant and said, well, it means what it means. And if they misinterpret it or they think it means something else, then that's their problem.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>但他有点挑衅地说，嗯，它的意思就是它的意思。如果他们误解了或者认为它意味着别的东西，那那是他们的问题。

