<v Jonathan Menjivar>Yeah, he wasn't trying to hide anything.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>是的，他并没有试图隐瞒什么。

00:32:13.890 --> 00:32:20.530
<v Lyric R. Cabral>No. I mean, he drove around town in a car that said Al-Shabaab Islamic Institute. Like, he picked up students in this vehicle.
<v Lyric R. Cabral>没有。我的意思是，他开着一辆写着“青年党伊斯兰学院”的车在城里转。就像，他用这辆车接学生。

00:32:20.530 --> 00:32:22.970
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Like on the side? What do you mean, it said it on the car?
<v Jonathan Menjivar>就像在侧面？什么意思，车身上写着？

00:32:22.970 --> 00:32:28.640
<v Lyric R. Cabral>Oh, we'll send you a Myspace picture. He literally-- like there's a picture of him posing by the vehicle with a child inside, and it says Al-Shabaab.
<v Lyric R. Cabral>哦，我们会发给你一张Myspace照片。他字面上——就像有一张他靠在车边的照片，里面有个孩子，上面写着“青年党”。

00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:32.790
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>Like a big magnetic sign that he'd kind of gotten made and slapped on the side of a minivan.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>就像房地产经纪人那种磁性标志，他让人做了然后拍在面包车侧面一样。

00:32:32.790 --> 00:32:35.200
<v Jonathan Menjivar>The way like a real estate agent does.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>就像房地产经纪人做的那样。

00:32:35.200 --> 00:32:35.630
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>Mhm.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>嗯。

00:32:35.630 --> 00:32:36.620
<v Lyric R. Cabral>Yes.
<v Lyric R. Cabral>是的。

00:32:36.620 --> 00:32:41.580
<v Lyric R. Cabral>[MUSIC PLAYING]
<v Lyric R. Cabral>[音乐播放]

00:32:41.580 --> 00:32:54.530
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Over the seven months David and Lyric were following Sharif through his investigation of Khalifa, they'd check in with him every other day or so, filming whenever they could-- in his safe house, on the street, while he was on the phone with his FBI handlers.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>在大卫和莉莉克跟踪谢里夫调查哈利法的七个月里，他们大约每隔一天就和他联系一次，只要有机会就拍摄——在他的安全屋，在街上，当他和FBI对接人通话时。

00:32:54.530 --> 00:33:08.200
<v Sharif>Yeah, what's up, Todd Exactly. I don't have bay'ah to this masjid, and I don't have bay'ah to the imam here, either. And most people, you have bay'ah to the imam. That way you can move around with them. I don't have it.
<v Sharif>是的，怎么了，托德。准确地说。我没有对这个清真寺效忠，我也没有对这里的伊玛目效忠。大多数人，你会对伊玛目效忠。这样你可以和他们一起行动。我没有。

00:33:08.200 --> 00:33:29.040
<v Jonathan Menjivar>It's such an intimate view of an informant's job. And what we see is how much of a counterterrorism investigation-- at least this case-- is really just someone trying very hard to make friends with a total stranger. So Sharif goes to the mosque, hoping to bump into Khalifa. He asks Khalifa out for coffee, offers him rides.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>这是一个对线人工作的深刻洞察。我们看到的是，反恐调查——至少在这个案件中——有多少真的只是一个人努力想和一个完全陌生的人交朋友。所以谢里夫去清真寺，希望能撞见哈利法。他约哈利法喝咖啡，主动提出载他一程。

00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:37.940
<v Jonathan Menjivar>And most of the time, Khalifa just ignores him. Sharif's over-eagerness in all of this is a little hard to watch. He's like the Ned Flanders of FBI stings.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>大多数时候，哈利法只是忽略他。谢里夫对这一切的过度渴望有点难以直视。他就像FBI钓鱼执法中的内德·弗兰德斯。

00:33:37.940 --> 00:33:54.620
<v Jonathan Menjivar>He's constantly texting Khalifa. For example, months into the investigation, Sharif sent Khalifa this text. "As-salaam alaikum, Brother K. What's up? Can you assist me in setting up laptops/Facebook? Inshallah." Here's Lyric.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>他不停地给哈利法发短信。例如，调查进行到几个月时，谢里夫给哈利法发了这条短信。“愿安拉赐你平安，K兄弟。怎么了？你能帮我设置一下笔记本电脑/Facebook吗？因沙安拉。”这是莉莉克。

00:33:54.620 --> 00:34:11.060
<v Lyric R. Cabral>You know, he's not supposed to know how to use Facebook at his age, and I think it was a-- the FBI made that suggestion for Sharif to ask Khalifa to help him set up his Facebook page as a way for Sharif to endear himself to Khalifa, in the sense of like, oh, I'm not knowledgeable in this area. Brother, can you please help me?
<v Lyric R. Cabral>你知道，他这个年纪本不应该知道怎么用Facebook，我认为这是一个——FBI给谢里夫提了建议，让他请哈利法帮忙设置Facebook主页，作为谢里夫赢得哈利法好感的一种方式，意思是，哦，我不懂这方面。兄弟，你能帮帮我吗？

00:34:11.060 --> 00:34:32.110
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Khalifa did not help his Muslim brother. In fact, after Sharif tried to friend Khalifa several times over months, Khalifa blocked him. Sharif then sent Khalifa a text that said, "Why didn't you answer my request? Since you blocked me, you have to request it from me." Khalifa texted back, "It's not that serious, bro. LOL."
<v Jonathan Menjivar>哈利法没有帮助他的穆斯林兄弟。事实上，在谢里夫几个月内多次尝试加哈利法好友后，哈利法屏蔽了他。谢里夫给哈利法发了一条短信，“你为什么不回答我的请求？既然你屏蔽了我，你得重新发请求给我。”哈利法回信，“没那么严重，哥们。哈哈。”

00:34:32.110 --> 00:34:36.380
<v Jonathan Menjivar>[MUSIC PLAYING]
<v Jonathan Menjivar>[音乐播放]

00:34:36.380 --> 00:34:49.790
<v Jonathan Menjivar>It's hard to see how the FBI thought this was ever supposed to work. Sharif was a lot older than Khalifa. His days as a revolutionary with the Black Panthers were decades ago, and not exactly relevant to a much younger white convert.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>很难看出FBI怎么会认为这能成功。谢里夫比哈利法大很多。他作为黑豹党革命者的日子已经是几十年前的事了，与一个年轻得多的白人皈依者并不相关。

00:34:49.790 --> 00:35:01.730
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Sharif smoked pot, dressed in street clothes. Khalifa proselytized and wore traditional Islamic garb. Lyric and David say Sharif was angry that the FBI hadn't done enough to make him seem believable.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>谢里夫抽大麻，穿街头服装。哈利法传教并穿传统的伊斯兰服饰。莉莉克和大卫说谢里夫很生气，因为FBI没能做更多让他看起来可信的事情。

00:35:01.730 --> 00:35:16.860
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>He was really frustrated that the FBI didn't have a cover for him. You know, he said, if I had been a businessman, I could have used that as an entryway and say, oh, Khalifa, you want to set up a shop. And Khalifa did want to set up a shop, I think, a breakfast cafe for people to go to after morning prayer.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>他真的很沮丧，FBI没有为他提供伪装。你知道，他说，如果我是一个商人，我就可以把它作为切入点，说，哦，哈利法，你想开一家店。哈利法确实想开一家店，我想，一个早晨祈祷后人们可以去吃的早餐咖啡馆。

00:35:16.860 --> 00:35:30.100
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>And Sharif would say, like, if I had a businessman cover, you know, I could use that as a way to kind of like to keep the conversation going and eventually get to a point where we're talking about money, and you know, what are you going to do for money? If I do this for you, what would you do for me?
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>谢里夫会说，如果我有商人伪装，你知道，我就可以用它作为一种让对话继续下去的方式，并最终达到一个点，我们谈论钱，你知道，你打算怎么赚钱？如果我为你做这个，你会为我做什么？

00:35:30.100 --> 00:35:43.450
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>There just wasn't like a specific foothold. There wasn't like anything specifically related to Sharif's cover that would initiate an organic conversation about these issues. From what I can tell, it seems to come out of left field every single time.
<v David Felix Sutcliffe>根本没有像具体的立足点。没有与谢里夫伪装相关的任何具体内容可以开启关于这些问题的有机对话。据我所知，它似乎每次都完全没来由。

00:35:43.450 --> 00:35:52.500
<v Jonathan Menjivar>For example, one day, as Sharif explains in the film, he was talking with Khalifa, and the classic holy war conversation-starter, camping, came up.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>例如，有一天，正如谢里夫在电影中解释的那样，他正在和哈利法交谈，经典的圣战对话开启者，露营，出现了。

00:35:52.500 --> 00:36:10.230
<v Sharif>That was my key opening right there.  The door opened up for me to make a suggestion now. I said, oh, that's cool, man. We could all go camping. I said, you know, why don't we just go a little further? We could train, man, like we do in the military.
<v Sharif>那是我的关键开场。门为我打开了，可以提建议了。我说，哦，太酷了，伙计。我们可以一起去露营。我说，你知道，为什么我们不走远一点？我们可以像在军队里那样训练。

00:36:10.230 --> 00:36:39.260
<v Sharif>I said, brother-- 'cause he wanted to go and fight for the Muslim State. He said, I gotta consult my sheikh. I said, see, that's what's wrong with you, brother. You brothers always talk that jihad stuff, but when somebody gives you the opportunity to make a move to fight for the Islam, y'all are not gonna fight for the Islam. Y'all talk that talk, but you won't walk the walk.
<v Sharif>我说，兄弟——因为他想去为穆斯林国家而战。他说，我得咨询我的谢赫。我说，看，这就是你的问题，兄弟。你们兄弟总是谈论那些圣战的事，但当有人给你机会采取行动为伊斯兰而战时，你们却不会为伊斯兰而战。你们光说不练。

00:36:39.260 --> 00:36:56.470
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Sharif was supposed to gather evidence, record his conversations for FBI analysis. But when he did manage to speak to Khalifa, he couldn't get Khalifa to say anything that Khalifa hadn't already revealed himself on his Facebook page. So he tried other methods that are familiar, if you've ever followed these kinds of cases.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>谢里夫本应收集证据，为FBI分析录下他的谈话。但当他确实设法和哈利法交谈时，他无法让哈利法说出任何哈利法没在Facebook主页上透露过的事情。所以他尝试了其他方法，如果你曾经关注过这类案件，你会很熟悉。

00:36:56.470 --> 00:37:06.090
<v Jonathan Menjivar>He asked Khalifa to buy him a gun. Sharif said that he needed protection from neighborhood kids who were selling drugs in front of his house. Khalifa didn't bite on that, either.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>他让哈利法给他买枪。谢里夫说他需要保护自己，免受在他家门前卖毒品的社区孩子的骚扰。哈利法也没吃这一套。

00:37:06.090 --> 00:37:16.300
<v Jonathan Menjivar>But the FBI wanted Sharif to keep going. He would text the FBI to tell them what he was up to. "Heading to Friday prayer at al-Noor Mosque. No word from POI."
<v Jonathan Menjivar>但FBI希望谢里夫继续努力。他会发短信给FBI告诉他们他在做什么。“正前往诺尔清真寺参加周五祈祷。POI没有消息。”

00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:24.210
<v Jonathan Menjivar>The FBI would text back, "POI just walked in. Turn recorder on before you go in. Talk to him a little. Get a feel."
<v Jonathan Menjivar>FBI会回信，“POI刚刚走进去。进去前打开录音机。和他聊聊。感觉一下。”

00:37:24.210 --> 00:37:28.640
<v President George W. Bush>Terrorists who commit these acts and those who harbor them.
<v President George W. Bush>实施这些行为的恐怖分子以及那些包庇他们的人。

00:37:28.640 --> 00:37:37.760
<v Jonathan Menjivar>One Sunday night, three months into the investigation, something happened that shows just how hard it is to appear authentic in a situation that's completely fake.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>一个周日晚上，调查进行了三个月，发生了一件事，表明在一个完全虚假的情况下表现得真实是多么困难。

00:37:37.760 --> 00:37:39.750
<v Woman On Tv>She wants out. She asked for--
<v Woman On Tv>她想退出。她问——

00:37:39.750 --> 00:37:57.730
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Lyric and David were filming Sharif in his apartment, watching TV, and Sharif sent this text. "ASA." That's short for As-salaam alaikum. "ASA, Brother K. Check this movie on channel 370, Showtime." And then in parentheses, Sharif adds, " Homeland ."
<v Jonathan Menjivar>莉莉克和大卫在谢里夫的公寓里拍他，看电视，谢里夫发了这条短信。“ASA。”那是“愿安拉赐你平安”的缩写。“愿安拉赐你平安，K兄弟。看看370频道Showtime上的这部电影。”然后在括号里，谢里夫补充说，“《国土安全》。”

00:37:57.730 --> 00:38:15.540
<v Jonathan Menjivar>Khalifa texts back, "Hm, on Netflix?" Sharif responds, "No, Showtime. It's called Homeland . Taliban Warrior." A 63-year-old former Black Panther with decades of experience as a government informant, and the thing he does is text his target about Homeland .
<v Jonathan Menjivar>哈利法回信，“嗯，Netflix上有吗？”谢里夫回复，“没有，Showtime。它叫《国土安全》。塔利班战士。”一个63岁的前黑豹党成员，有几十年的政府线人经验，他做的事情竟然是发短信给他的目标谈论《国土安全》。

00:38:15.540 --> 00:38:22.360
<v Jonathan Menjivar>[MUSIC PLAYING]
<v Jonathan Menjivar>[音乐播放]

00:38:22.360 --> 00:38:36.310
<v Jonathan Menjivar>By late January 2012, four months into Sharif's involvement in the investigation, Khalifa still hadn't said or done anything that the FBI could use to charge him. No support for terrorism, no plans to engage in any illegal activity.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>到2012年1月下旬，谢里夫参与调查四个月后，哈利法仍然没有说或做任何FBI可以用来指控他的事情。没有对恐怖主义的支持，没有参与任何非法活动的计划。

00:38:36.310 --> 00:38:48.420
<v Jonathan Menjivar>And then one day, Lyric and David saw something on Khalifa's Facebook page that made it clear that this whole game was make-believe. This idea that Sharif was some kind of terrorist recruiter was crumbling.
<v Jonathan Menjivar>然后有一天，莉莉克和大卫在哈利法的Facebook主页上看到了让这一切明显是虚构的东西。谢里夫是某种恐怖主义招募者的想法正在崩溃。

00:38:48.420 --> 00:39:02.480
<v Lyric R. Cabral>Um, I believe his first sort of public inkling that something was wrong, he wrote, "The Feds must think I'm Willie Lump Lump. They think they can send anyone to me." And we knew that that was an indirect reference to Sharif on the ground in Pittsburgh.
<v Lyric R. Cabral>嗯，我相信他第一个公开的暗示是出了问题，他写道，“联邦调查局一定以为我是‘威利·伦普·伦普’。他们以为可以随便派个人来找我。”我们知道那是对匹兹堡当地谢里夫的间接指涉。

00:39:02.480 --> 00:39:18.120
<v Jonathan Menjivar>And then on March 9, 2012, Khalifa posted the following, which he also sent out via email to a bunch of reporters. Quote, "Sometime in September or October of 2011, I met Saeed S. Torres, who introduced himself to me as Sharif."
